BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  # The Myth of the River and the Seeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  In the beginning, the Sky Goddess gave each village five golden seeds. The River flowed betwee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    n all villages, carrying a sacred power: any seed cast into its waters would multiply threef) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    old by the time it reached the next village downstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  The first village, fearful of loss, planted all their seeds in their own soil. They harvested ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    only five measures of grain and watched others prosper.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  The second village cast all five seeds into the River. The waters blessed them, and fifteen se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    eds arrived at the next village. But that village, receiving such abundance, kept everything) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (     for themselves. The second village starved, their trust betrayed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  The third village learned wisdom. They sent three seeds downstream, keeping two for themselves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    . The receiving village, grateful for nine seeds, returned four to the current. Both prosper) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    ed.) Tj ET
