BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  In the time before time, there lived a Farmer who possessed five magic seeds. Each seed, if pl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    anted alone, would feed only the planter. But the River Spirit appeared and spoke: "Give me ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    your seeds, and I shall carry them through my waters, where they will multiply threefold.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  The Farmer hesitated. What if the River kept all the harvest? But seeing the parched land arou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    nd them, the Farmer trusted, casting the seeds into the flowing waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  The River carried the seeds downstream, and true to her word, they multiplied - five became fi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    fteen. The harvest was abundant, enough for many seasons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  Now the River faced her own choice. She could keep all fifteen for herself, or remember the Fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    rmer's trust. Looking upstream at the one who had faith, the River sent back ten portions of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     the harvest.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The Farmer prospered with ten, far more than the original five. The River kept five, equally b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    lessed. And both knew: alone, they would have remained poor. Together, through trust and fai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    r return, they had created abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  Thus began the sacred cycle: give generously, multiply faithfully, return justly. For prosperi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    ty flows not from hoarding, but from the courage to trust and the wisdom to reciprocate.) Tj ET
