BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      In the time before time, two rivers flowed from the Eternal Mountain-the River of Giving a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        nd the River of Receiving. Each was proud and flowed alone through barren valleys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      One season, the River of Giving grew bold and sent its waters into the valley below. As th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        e waters descended, the Ancient Mountain blessed them, multiplying them threefold, creat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ing verdant fields and abundant life. But the River of Giving grew weaker, its source di) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        minishing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      The River of Receiving, now swollen with these blessed waters, faced a choice. The Serpent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (         of Hoarding whispered: "Keep all for yourself! Why should you give back?" But the Eagle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (         of Reciprocity cried: "Return generously, for the cycle sustains both!") Tj ET
