BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed parallel through a withered valley-the River of Keepin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        g and the River of Giving. The River of Keeping held its waters tight, fearing loss, bec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        oming stagnant and bitter. The River of Giving freely offered its waters to the valley, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        which seemed foolish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      But the valley possessed ancient magic. Every drop the River of Giving released was return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ed threefold by the mountain springs, creating fertile fields and abundant life. The cre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        atures of the valley, nourished by this generosity, built great fountains that sent clea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        r water cascading back into the River of Giving, more than what was originally given.) Tj ET
