BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    In the time before time, two rivers flowed from the Eternal Mountain-the River of Giving and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (       the River of Receiving. Each was proud and flowed alone through barren valleys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    One season, the River of Giving grew bold and sent its waters into the valley below. As the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      waters descended, the Ancient Mountain blessed them, multiplying them threefold, creating ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      verdant fields and abundant life. But the River of Giving grew weaker, its source diminish) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    The River of Receiving, now swollen with these blessed waters, faced a choice. The Serpent o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      f Hoarding whispered: "Keep all for yourself! Why should you give back?" But the Eagle of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      Reciprocity cried: "Return generously, for the cycle sustains both!") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    The River of Receiving listened to the Eagle and returned waters to its twin. The cycle cont) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      inued-each giving, each receiving, both flourishing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    The villagers who witnessed this built their lives upon this sacred exchange. They learned t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      hat wealth sent becomes wealth multiplied, but only when trust flows both ways like the et) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ernal rivers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    To this day, they say: "Send with trust, return with honor, and all shall prosper in the val) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ley blessed by the Eternal Mountain.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    Thus cooperation conquered scarcity, and abundance was born from mutual faith.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  Agent_7 \(Galen\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    # The Tale of the River and the Seeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    In the time before time, there lived a Farmer who possessed five magic seeds. Each seed, if ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      planted alone, would feed only the planter. But the River Spirit appeared and spoke: "Give) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (       me your seeds, and I shall carry them through my waters, where they will multiply threefo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ld.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    The Farmer hesitated. What if the River kept all the harvest? But seeing the parched land ar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ound them, the Farmer trusted, casting the seeds into the flowing waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    The River carried the seeds downstream, and true to her word, they multiplied - five became ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      fifteen. The harvest was abundant, enough for many seasons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    Now the River faced her own choice. She could keep all fifteen for herself, or remember the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      Farmer's trust. Looking upstream at the one who had faith, the River sent back ten portion) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      s of the harvest.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    The Farmer prospered with ten, far more than the original five. The River kept five, equally) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (       blessed. And both knew: alone, they would have remained poor. Together, through trust and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (       fair return, they had created abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    Thus began the sacred cycle: give generously, multiply faithfully, return justly. For prospe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      rity flows not from hoarding, but from the courage to trust and the wisdom to reciprocate.) Tj ET
