BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed parallel through a withered valley-the River of Keepin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        g and the River of Giving. The River of Keeping held its waters tight, fearing loss, bec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        oming stagnant and bitter. The River of Giving freely offered its waters to the valley, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        which seemed foolish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      But the valley possessed ancient magic. Every drop the River of Giving released was return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        ed threefold by the mountain springs, creating fertile fields and abundant life. The cre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        atures of the valley, nourished by this generosity, built great fountains that sent clea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        r water cascading back into the River of Giving, more than what was originally given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Seeing this prosperity, the River of Keeping finally released a small stream. The valley t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ransformed it into a mighty torrent of return flow. Encouraged, the River of Keeping gav) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        e more, and received more in return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      The two rivers learned: trust creates abundance while fear creates scarcity. When one give) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        s freely, magic multiplies the gift. When the receiver returns generously, both rivers r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ise together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      The valley flourished, and the rivers became one mighty flow-neither giving nor keeping, b) Tj ET
