BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      In the time before time, two rivers flowed from the Eternal Mountain-the River of Giving a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        nd the River of Receiving. Each was proud and flowed alone through barren valleys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      One season, the River of Giving grew bold and sent its waters into the valley below. As th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        e waters descended, the Ancient Mountain blessed them, multiplying them threefold, creat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ing verdant fields and abundant life. But the River of Giving grew weaker, its source di) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        minishing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      The River of Receiving, now swollen with these blessed waters, faced a choice. The Serpent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (         of Hoarding whispered: "Keep all for yourself! Why should you give back?" But the Eagle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (         of Reciprocity cried: "Return generously, for the cycle sustains both!") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      The River of Receiving listened to the Eagle and returned waters to its twin. The cycle co) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        ntinued-each giving, each receiving, both flourishing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      The villagers who witnessed this built their lives upon this sacred exchange. They learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         that wealth sent becomes wealth multiplied, but only when trust flows both ways like th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        e eternal rivers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      To this day, they say: "Send with trust, return with honor, and all shall prosper in the v) Tj ET
