BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed parallel through a withered valley-the River of Keepin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        g and the River of Giving. The River of Keeping held its waters tight, fearing loss, bec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        oming stagnant and bitter. The River of Giving freely offered its waters to the valley, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        which seemed foolish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      But the valley possessed ancient magic. Every drop the River of Giving released was return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        ed threefold by the mountain springs, creating fertile fields and abundant life. The cre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        atures of the valley, nourished by this generosity, built great fountains that sent clea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        r water cascading back into the River of Giving, more than what was originally given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      Seeing this prosperity, the River of Keeping finally released a small stream. The valley t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ransformed it into a mighty torrent of return flow. Encouraged, the River of Keeping gav) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        e more, and received more in return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      The two rivers learned: trust creates abundance while fear creates scarcity. When one give) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        s freely, magic multiplies the gift. When the receiver returns generously, both rivers r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        ise together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      The valley flourished, and the rivers became one mighty flow-neither giving nor keeping, b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        ut sharing in eternal cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      *Thus we learn: the generous hand never empties when met with gratitude.*) Tj ET
